% ============================================================================
% landforms.query.adj — a worked recall over the geography landforms library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what defines a canyon?":
% it states no geography fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `landform_description` rows and returns the descriptor + the table's source/
% locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% descriptor `deep_narrow`, recall its landform — canyon). A word that is not
% one of these landforms abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% descriptor.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli landforms.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "landforms.adj"

? landform_description(mountain, $Desc)      % expect projects_above_surroundings
? landform_description(canyon, $Desc)        % expect deep_narrow
? landform_description(plateau, $Desc)       % expect flat_elevated
? landform_description($Landform, deep_narrow) % reverse bind — expect canyon
? landform_description(ocean, $Desc)         % expect abstain — an ocean is a body of water, not a landform
